<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SCREEN COPY IS ENGLISH. FAILURE COPY IS BILINGUAL.

  v1 showed English and Tagalog together on every label. The v2 design
  (Attendance App - Redesign v2.dc.html) is English throughout, with
  shorter, plainer sentences doing the work the second line used to do
  ("Tap to start your day", "Pick the site you are working on").

  The _tl strings that remain are deliberate and are NOT leftovers. They
  all belong to refusals and errors — the messages where being misread
  costs the most, and the only ones the design never draws. See
  FailureNotice and AttendanceFailureNotice.

  Do NOT move the _tl strings into values-fil/. They are part of the
  message, shown alongside the English, not a translation of it.
-->
